{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013RTADtQaKW2h77jEdMnQ6T","type":"tool_result","content":"title:\t[INVESTIGATING] ecommerce-api elevated error rate (33%)\nstate:\tDRAFT\nauthor:\thar-ki (Harikiran Nayak)\nlabels:\tincident-fp:6e14cf73, incident:active, incident:investigating\nassignees:\t\nreviewers:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nnumber:\t4\nurl:\thttps://github.com/har-ki/claude-code-sre-handbook/pull/4\nadditions:\t0\ndeletions:\t0\nauto-merge:\tdisabled\n--\n## Trigger\n- **When:** 2026-05-19T22:11:47.304595+00:00\n- **Window:** 1-minute lookback\n- **Error rate at trigger:** 33%\n- **Samples in window:** 264\n- **Threshold:** 15%\n\n## Investigation\n\n### Error rate reconciliation\nThe watcher fired at **33%** over a 1-minute window (22:11 UTC). Over the full 15-minute observation window the blended rate is **21.46%** (822 errors / 3,830 total log events). The discrepancy is expected: error rate climbed over time as more products exhausted their in-memory stock, peaking at **35.7% at 22:11** (95 errors / 266 events) before continuing upward.\n\n### Top error class\n**100% of errors** are `Checkout failed: Insufficient stock for <product> (…): requested N, available M` logged at `ERROR` severity from the `POST /api/checkout` endpoint (HTTP 409 CONFLICT). No 500-level errors, panics, or OOM events were observed.\n\n### Affected products (last 15 min)\n| Product | Errors | Share |\n|---|---|---|\n| Ceramic Plant Pot (ID 7) | 808 | 92.7% |\n| Cotton T-Shirt (ID 4) | 13 | 1.5% |\n| Running Shoes (ID 6) | 11 | 1.3% |\n| Winter Jacket (ID 11) | 10 | 1.1% |\n| Smart Watch (ID 2) | 10 | 1.1% |\n| Others (IDs 1,3,5,8) | 29 | 3.3% |\n\n### Error timeline (errors / total per minute)\n| Minute (UTC) | Total | Errors | Rate |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 21:59 | 118 | 20 | 16.9% |\n| 22:00 | 330 | 68 | 20.6% |\n| 22:01–22:09 | ~295 avg | ~63 avg | ~21% |\n| 22:10 | 302 | 75 | 24.8% |\n| 22:11 | 266 | 95 | **35.7%** ← watcher fired |\n| 22:12 (partial) | 120 | 58 | 48.3% |\n\nError rate is trending upward as more products exhaust their in-memory stock.\n\n### Root cause: TOCTOU race in in-memory inventory\n\n**`otel-demo/ecommerce/backend/src/services/inventory.js`**\n\nThe in-memory inventory is initialized at startup with:\n```js\n// inventory.js:15-19\nconst inventory = {\n  1: 50, 2: 50, 3: 50, 4: 50, 5: 50, 6: 50,\n  7: 5,      // Ceramic Plant Pot — limited stock\n  8: 50, ...\n};\n```\n\nProduct 7 (Ceramic Plant Pot) starts with **5 units** vs. 50 for every other product, making it the first to deplete under load.\n\n`reserveInventory()` has a classic **Time-Of-Check / Time-Of-Use (TOCTOU) race**:\n\n```js\n// inventory.js:39-55 (simplified)\nconst currentStock = await getStock(item.id);          // reads inventory[id] + 5ms delay\nif (currentStock < item.quantity) throw InsufficientStock; // check\n\nawait new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 50 + Math.random() * 100)); // 50-150ms gap\n\ninventory[item.id] -= item.quantity;  // write — no lock held\n```\n\nUnder concurrent load, multiple requests can all read `stock=5` and all pass the check, then each decrement: `5 - N_concurrent` → **negative stock**. The `available -3` in log lines confirms product 7 was oversold by 3 units. Once `inventory[7]` is ≤ 0, every subsequent checkout attempt immediately fails the stock check and returns 409.\n\n### Trace evidence\nRepresentative failing trace: **`f6d3d993a82f4247e41ddb75dd842523`** (2026-05-19 22:12:07 UTC)\n- Root span: `POST /api/checkout` — `http.status_code: 409`, `order.id: ORD-E9CD358E`\n- Child span: `reserveInventory` — `StatusCode: Error`, `StatusMessage: \"Insufficient stock for product 2 (Smart Watch): requested 1, available 0\"`, `product.2.stock_before: 0`, `Duration: 6.4ms`\n- The `reserveInventory` span is the only error span; payment and other steps are never reached.\n\n### Kubernetes pod health\n`ecommerce-api-7c7f4fd679-hc8dz` in namespace `ecommerce`:\n- **Status:** Running, Ready 1/1\n- **Restarts:** 0\n- **OOM:** None — pod QoS is BestEffort but no resource pressure observed\n- **Events:** Normal startup only (Scheduled, Pulled, Created, Started at 21:59 UTC)\n\nThe pod is healthy. The incident is **entirely application-logic**, not infrastructure.\n\n### Summary\nThe root cause is a TOCTOU race in `inventory.js:reserveInventory()`: there is no mutex or atomic compare-and-swap guarding the read→check→decrement sequence. Product 7 (Ceramic Plant Pot) depleted first because it was initialized with only 5 units. Once oversold to -3, it generates a flood of 409s that are driving the error rate above threshold. Other products are also beginning to deplete, which explains the rising trend.\n\n## Proposed fix\n_Phase 2 will fill this in._\n\n## Incident report\n_Linked at `docs/incidents/2026-05-19-6e14cf73.md` after Phase 2._","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"db01e696-0c20-4de9-81e0-b4a28df6d14c","uuid":"85ea9391-1a7d-4ffc-a034-a060891e8e33","timestamp":"2026-05-19T22:14:08.944Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"title:\t[INVESTIGATING] ecommerce-api elevated error rate (33%)\nstate:\tDRAFT\nauthor:\thar-ki (Harikiran Nayak)\nlabels:\tincident-fp:6e14cf73, incident:active, incident:investigating\nassignees:\t\nreviewers:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nnumber:\t4\nurl:\thttps://github.com/har-ki/claude-code-sre-handbook/pull/4\nadditions:\t0\ndeletions:\t0\nauto-merge:\tdisabled\n--\n## Trigger\n- **When:** 2026-05-19T22:11:47.304595+00:00\n- **Window:** 1-minute lookback\n- **Error rate at trigger:** 33%\n- **Samples in window:** 264\n- **Threshold:** 15%\n\n## Investigation\n\n### Error rate reconciliation\nThe watcher fired at **33%** over a 1-minute window (22:11 UTC). Over the full 15-minute observation window the blended rate is **21.46%** (822 errors / 3,830 total log events). The discrepancy is expected: error rate climbed over time as more products exhausted their in-memory stock, peaking at **35.7% at 22:11